## Why This Is Asked
Tests stateful cross-topic streaming, per-key windowing, offset management, and recovery semantics within KCNA.

## Key Concepts
- Stateful cross-topic join for userId
- Per-topic offset preservation and replay safety
- 15-second tumbling window with watermark handling
- State snapshotting to a compacted 'kcna_state' topic
- Exactly-once vs at-least-once emission guarantees and dedup

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: join processor sketch
class JoinProcessor {
  constructor() {
    this.profileCache = new Map();
    this.window = new TumblingWindow(15); // in seconds
  }
  onClick(click) {
    const pid = this.profileCache.get(click.userId);
    if (pid) emitEnriched({ ...click, profileVersion: pid.version });
    // else stash or wait for profile
  }
  onProfile(profile) {
    this.profileCache.set(profile.userId, profile);
  }
  onWindowEmit(windowId) {
    // snapshot state to kcna_state and commit
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests stateful per-key windowing, dynamic rule handling, and exactly-once guarantees under late messages.

## Key Concepts
- Per-account sliding window sums
- Dynamic rule lookup and on-the-fly threshold changes
- Watermarks for late arrivals and eviction
- Exactly-once semantics and idempotent fraud_alerts
- Backpressure and test canary design

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: per-account rolling sum with 5m sliding window
state = Map(); // accountId -> [{ts, amt}]
rules = Map(); // accountId -> threshold
onEvent(tx) {
  cleanExpired(tx.ts);
  sum = sumAmt(state.get(tx.accountId));
  threshold = rules.get(tx.accountId) ?? default;
  if (sum > threshold) emitFraud(tx.accountId, sum, threshold);
  append(state, tx.accountId, {ts: tx.ts, amt: tx.amount});
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle simultaneous rule updates and transactions to avoid inconsistent alerts?
- How would you scale to millions of accounts and high-throughput streams while maintaining low latency?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests expertise in geo-distributed, multi-tenant governance covering data residency requirements, cross-data center ordering guarantees, and traffic optimization under production load.

## Key Concepts

- Geo-distributed multi-tenant isolation and compliance
- Region-aware partitioning and leader election
- Cross-region replication throttling and causal ordering
- Canary rollout strategies and rollback mechanisms
- Compliance auditing and residency enforcement

## Code Example

```javascript
// Implementation sketch
class GeoPolicy {
  constructor(tenantRegionMap) { this.tenantRegionMap = tenantRegionMap; }

  getRegionsForTenant(tenantId) {
    return this.tenantRegionMap[tenantId] || ['default'];
  }

  enforceResidency(tenantId, targetRegion) {
    const allowedRegions = this.getRegionsForTenant(tenantId);
    return allowedRegions.includes(targetRegion);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle tenant region migrations with zero downtime?
- What monitoring metrics would you track for geo-replication health?
- How do you ensure consistency during network partitions?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a practical KCNA routing pattern: per-message fan-out with per-destination ordering and safe offset commits.

## Key Concepts
- Per-destination routing and ordering
- Offset management: commit after downstream ack
- Outbox pattern and idempotent sinks
- Retries and backoff
- Canary testing for correctness

## Code Example
```javascript
class RouteFanoutProcessor {
  onMessage(msg) {
    const dest = msg.headers.dest;
    const target = `sink-${dest}`;
    return publish(target, msg.payload).then(() => ack(msg.offset));
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale to many destinations and hot keys?
- How would you guarantee approximate exactly-once with external sinks?
- How would you instrument latency and ordering per destination?

